# Git Workflow: Main Branch Only

This project works exclusively on the `main` branch. Do not create feature/topic branches.

- Always make commits directly on `main`. Do not run `git checkout -b <name>` or `git branch <name>` to create new branches.
- Before committing, verify the current branch is `main` (`git branch --show-current`). If not, switch to `main` first (after handling any in-progress work).
- Do not open pull requests for new work; commit and push straight to `main`.
- Do not create git worktrees on new branches.
- If asked to review or merge existing PRs from legacy branches, merge into `main` and then delete the source branch (local and remote) to keep the branch list clean.
- Exception: only create a separate branch if the user explicitly asks for one by name.
